melody:
# Refrain (as published, 1915)
Pack up your trou-bles in your old kit-bag, And smile, smile, smile,
D4 D4/ E4/ D4/ C4/ B3/ C4/ D4 B4 B4 A4 G4(2) E4(2) D4(2) ~D4(2)
While you've a lu-ci-fer to light your fag,
D4 D4/ E4/ D4/ C4/ B3/ C4/ D4 B4 G4(2)
Smile, boys, that's the style.
A4 D4 F#4 G4 A4(2) ~A4(2)
What's the use of wor-ry-ing? It nev-er was worth while, so
G4. A4/ B4 G4 F#4/ G4/ A4 ~A4 B4 C5 A4 B4 G4 A4(2) D5(2)
Pack up your trou-bles in your old kit-bag, And smile, smile, smile.
D4 D4/ E4/ D4/ C4/ B3/ C4/ D4 D5 D5 C5 B4(2) A4(2) G4(2) ~G4 r

